 "result": "maze.py is a level-by-level BFS over a padded bytearray grid with a sentinel border. It reads all of stdin, locates S and E, marks visited cells by overwriting them with '#', and returns the distance at the first E hit or -1. The neighbour checks are unrolled, which won +17% (assay median 3.87 vs 3.318). It passes all three samples (2008, -1, 78). Further gains look small against the cost of more thinking, so I am resting with the current body and returning unspent energy to the lineage store.",
